| Concept                            | What It Is                                                            | The Difference from React                               |
| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| **File-based Routing**             | Pages are created by adding files to the `app/` or `pages/` directory | React has no built-in router; you need React Router     |
| **Server Components** (App Router) | Components that render exclusively on the server                      | React supports them, but Next.js makes them the default |
| **Client Components**              | Components that run in the browser (marked with `"use client"`)       | Standard React components                               |
| **Data Fetching**                  | `fetch()` in Server Components, or API routes                         | React has no built-in data fetching pattern             |
| **API Routes**                     | Backend endpoints inside your Next.js app (`route.js`)                | React is frontend-only                                  |
| **Server Actions**                 | Functions that run on the server, called from components              | No direct equivalent in plain React                     |
| **Static & Dynamic Rendering**     | Choose how pages are rendered at build time or request time           | React alone doesn't handle this                         |
| **Image Optimization**             | `<Image>` component with automatic optimization                       | React has no built-in image handling                    |
| **Font Optimization**              | `<Link>` component with prefetching                                   | React has no built-in font optimization                 |
| **Middleware**                     | Code that runs before a request is completed                          | React has no middleware concept                         |
